      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOWDY MATE (4) has been freshened since the Victoria Derby where he started favourite and led but faded to finish midfield. He was racing very well with a string of top-two results here prior. A drop in both class and distance gives him every chance to return to winning form. RUBYS DREAM (7) has won the last three times she raced over this distance here, leading and digging deep to get home by a neck last time. Tactics will be crucial from this wide draw but she is going well. KEAYANG KURKI (5) overcame a back row draw for a last-start win by 5.4 metres at Maryborough. She could go on with it. CHARLESTON AVENUE (2) is up in grade but draws much better than he did when placed here last week.",
